To register a hook, you need to specify the delegate type and the method you want to call.

ISimpleHookService.RegisterHook<PluginOnPreUpdateDelegate>(MyOnPreUpdate);

public static void MyOnPreUpdate(float deltaTime) { /* Do something */ }

You may also use a lambda expression to register a hook:

ISimpleHookService.RegisterHook<PluginOnPreUpdateDelegate>(deltaTime => { /* Do something */ });

Using a lambda this way doesn't  allow you to manually deregister the hook on your own using 
unless you store a reference to the lambda in a variable, but at that point you might as well use a method.
Regardless the game will still automatically deregister everything when your plugin is unloaded.

To deregister a hook:

ISimpleHookService.DeregisterHook(MyOnPreUpdate);

You may omit the generic type as the reference to the callback is used to find and deregister it.

You can create new status effect actions by implementing the interface :

public class FooAction : IStatusEffectAction
{
    private readonly string _message;

    public FooAction(StatusEffect statusEffect, XElement element)
    {
        _message = element.GetAttributeString("message", "");
    }

    public void Apply(StatusEffectParams effectParams)
    {
        if (!_message.IsNullOrEmpty())
        {
            DebugConsole.NewMessage(_message);
        }
    }
}

And to register the type, you can use the built-in factory implementation :

StatusEffectService.RegisterAction(new StatusEffectActionFactory("Foo", (StatusEffect statusEffect, XElement element) => new FooAction(statusEffect, element)));

Now you can use your new custom action in status effects:

<StatusEffect ...>
  <Foo message="Test" />
</StatusEffect>

Interface declaration:

public interface IExampleService : IPluginService { }
public interface IExampleTransientService : IPluginService { }

Simple singleton implementation:

internal sealed class ImplExampleService : IExampleService { }

Transient implementation, implement  along with our service interface:

internal sealed class ImplExampleTransientService : ITransientService, IExampleTransientService
{
    public ImplExampleTransientService(PluginData data, Assembly assembly)
        => PluginLoader.AddTransientService(assembly, this);

    public void Dispose() { /* Dispose resources */ }
}

PluginServiceProvider.cs:

  private static readonly PluginServiceProvider Services =
    new PluginServiceBuilder()
        .AddSingleton<IExampleService, ImplExampleService>()
        .AddTransient<IExampleTransientService>(CreateTransient<ImplExampleTransientService>)
        .Build();

